{
  "id": "ticket_01KYAVM4GJVG34MC95VDNT7JVQ",
  "name": "web: mtime-keyed cross-request cache for FixtureDataSource directory scans",
  "slug": "web-mtime-keyed-cross-request",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "web: mtime-keyed cross-request cache for FixtureDataSource directory scans",
    "details_md": "web-every-request-full-rescans fixed the within-a-single-request double-scans (tickets scanned twice via findTicketByRef+listTickets, sessions scanned twice via listSessionsForTicket+listEventsForTicket) but deliberately left cross-request caching out of scope: every request still fully re-reads+parses the tickets/sessions/events directories from scratch, even when nothing on disk changed since the last request. Fine at hundreds of tickets; noticeable at 1k+, especially a big events dir (every view but transcript-view.ts calls something that scans it). A later work item should add an mtime-keyed (or content-digest-keyed, matching repo/db-index.ts A3 precedent) in-memory cache in FixtureDataSource, invalidated when a directory's mtime (or per-file mtimes) changes, so a run of requests against an unchanged .slop/db pays the scan cost once, not once per request.",
    "acceptance": [
      "repeated requests against an unchanged .slop/db do not re-read+re-parse every ticket/session/event file each time",
      "a write to .slop/db between requests (e.g. a concurrent slop CLI command) is still reflected on the next request, not served stale"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/web/fixture-data-source.ts",
      "src/repo/db-index.ts (existing content-digest fingerprint precedent, A3)"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
  },
